# SYNTHETIC, not a real connector. Exercises the ONE arm of
# `integer_bound` (src/form_schema.rs) that no other fixture reaches: a
# declared sh:minInclusive / sh:maxInclusive that will not parse as an
# integer, on a field whose sh:datatype is an integer type (phase F item
# W4, contreforts/contreforts-core#34; gap found in review, a3).
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS AND WHY IT IS NOT COVERED ELSEWHERE. `PropertyShape`
# keeps a bound as its literal's RAW LEXICAL FORM, deliberately -- that
# layer does not know the property's range and will not narrow it. The
# digest is where the range is known, so the digest is where the parse
# happens, and a bound the digest cannot parse is a declared constraint
# the rendered form would silently not enforce. Dropping it to `None`
# would produce an unbounded number box for a field the declaration
# bounded -- the exact "absence presenting as success" shape this whole
# item exists to close. Silencing the error arm left the whole suite
# green -- measured -- so before this file the arm was unreviewed code.
#
# ZERO INSTANCES TREE-WIDE: all five sh:minInclusive/sh:maxInclusive
# objects in the tree (stalwart:listenPort, smtpLocalPort, smtpRelayPort,
# ollamaTimeoutSecs, and this directory's own datatype-controls fixture)
# are plain xsd:integer literals. `1.5` below is an xsd:decimal, which is
# the realistic way this arrives: a bound written with a decimal point on
# a field declared xsd:integer.
@prefix rdfs:         <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:           <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:          <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix contreforts:  <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/declaration#> .
@prefix nib:          <https://contreforts.ds-labs.org/ontologies/non-integer-bound-test#> .

nib:NonIntegerBoundConnectorShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass nib:NonIntegerBoundConnector ;
    contreforts:category "test-only" ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path nib:label ;
        sh:name "Label" ;
        sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:group nib:GeneralGroup ;
        sh:order 1 ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path nib:listenPort ;
        sh:name "Listen port" ;
        sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
        # Not an integer. The field IS an integer field, so this bound is
        # meant to be enforced and cannot simply be ignored.
        sh:minInclusive 1.5 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:group nib:GeneralGroup ;
        sh:order 2 ;
    ] .

nib:GeneralGroup a sh:PropertyGroup ;
    rdfs:label "General" ;
    sh:order 1 .
